  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mercy Corps Catalysing Economic Development of Informal Sector CEDIS 2022-2026</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Mercy Corps Catalysing Economic Development of Informal Sector CEDIS 2022-2026</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Goal

About 30,000 vulnerable mostly young women in the urban and surrounding rural areas of Bulawayo, Mutare and Harare have improved incomes, working conditions and resilience to shocks and stresses through sustainable informal microenterprise livelihoods. 

Expected Results/Outcomes

1. Increased women&apos;s microenterprise access to markets and market services
2. Increased women&apos;s empowerment in the informal economy
3. Improved enabling environment for women in the informal economy</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">F&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrade f&#xf6;ruts&#xe4;ttningar f&#xf6;r produktiv
syssels&#xe4;ttning med anst&#xe4;ndiga arbetsvillkor
F&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrad anpassningsf&#xf6;rm&#xe5;ga och st&#xe4;rkt
motst&#xe5;ndskraft mot klimatf&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndringar och milj&#xf6; och naturkatastrofer, samt &#xf6;kad tillg&#xe5;ng till f&#xf6;rnybar energi och en h&#xf6;gre nergieffektivitet
&#xd6;kad j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet, inklusive &#xe5;tnjutande av och
respekt f&#xf6;r sexuell och reproduktiv h&#xe4;lsa och
r&#xe4;ttigheter (SRHR)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved conditions for productive employment with decent working conditions. Improved adaptability and strengthened resilience to climate change and the environment and natural disasters, as well as increased access to renewable energy and higher energy efficiency. Increased equality, including the enjoyment of and respect for sexual and reproductive health and rights (SRHR).</narrative>
  </description>
